Package: golemcat
Title: Computerized Adaptive Testing of the Big Five with the Rating Scale Model
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Dimitrios", "Zacharatos", email = "dzacharatos@yahoo.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Maintainer: Dimitrios Zacharatos <dzacharatos@yahoo.com>
Description: A 'shiny' application, built as a 'golem' package, that gives the
    50 statements of the IPIP Big-Five Factor Markers as a computerized
    adaptive test (CAT). Each trait is scored with the rating scale model,
    the next statement is the one with the most Fisher information at the
    current expected a posteriori (EAP) estimate, and a trait stops when its
    standard error reaches a threshold. One tab is the questionnaire as a
    respondent sees it, with a profile of the five traits at the end; another
    shows the workings of the CAT after every answer. The engine, which gives
    the same results as 'catR', and the session logic are also R functions,
    and any item bank fitted with the rating scale model of 'mirt' can be read.
License: GPL-3
URL: https://github.com/sedzinfo/golemcat
BugReports: https://github.com/sedzinfo/golemcat/issues
